vkd3d: Requiem clamps the wave size in most places, and the rest is the bug.

**docs/TODO.md #56, and this is the mechanism the entry never had.** Five
compute shaders were dumped from the broken scene and disassembled. Three are
`LocalSize 32 1 1`, and they read `WaveGetLaneCount()` six times: three reads go
through `UMin(32, SubgroupSize)`, and the load-bearing ones do not.

    %402 = OpLoad %uint %SubgroupSize        ; raw
    %403 = OpIMul %uint %402 %401            ; base   = waveSize * groupIdx
    %513 = OpIAdd %uint %509 %138            ; + WavePrefixCountBits(true), 0..31
    %540 = OpIAdd %uint %539 %402            ; stride by waveSize

The shader means wave size to equal the group size. **On this device it is
double that.** `threadsize_base` defaults to 64 (`freedreno_dev_info.py:108`)
and neither `a7xx_base` nor `a8xx_base` overrides it, so Turnip reports
`minSubgroupSize == maxSubgroupSize == 64`. Lane ranks then cover 0..31 of a
window advanced by 64, and `ceil(count / 64)` dispatches half the groups:
**exactly every second item is never processed.**

That is the symptom, precisely. Deterministic, because it is arithmetic. The
objects still exist to the CPU, so collision holds against walls that never
draw. Nothing logs an error, because nothing is wrong -- the shader ran and did
what it was told. And only *some* geometry disappears, because the two
`LocalSize 128` shaders in the same set clamp to 128 and are correct. Desktop
never sees it: NVIDIA reports 32, and RADV picks wave32 for small compute
groups.

vkd3d cannot fix it by asking for a narrower subgroup. The shaders carry no
`WaveSize` metadata, so `state.c` prepends no `requiredSubgroupSize`, and
`32 % 64 != 0` keeps `REQUIRE_FULL_SUBGROUPS` off as well.

**Upstream already fixed this for PRAGMATA, and this shares that entry rather
than adding a second one.** All five shaders dumped from Requiem carry the entry
point name `PersistentClusterCulling` -- byte-identical to the one PRAGMATA
matches, because it is RE Engine's own culling pass and not anything per-game.
So `pragmata_hashes` becomes `re_engine_hashes`, and both executables point at
it.

**Matching the shader rather than the executable is the point.** A per-game
entry fixes one game; matching `PersistentClusterCulling` covers PRAGMATA,
Requiem, and any later RE Engine title shipping the pass unchanged, without
anyone having to notice. It is also narrower than the alternative: applying the
clamp globally per-executable would rewrite `WaveGetLaneCount()` in every
32-thread compute shader the game has, including the ones that were written
correctly.

`ENABLE_FAIR_SCHEDULING` comes with it, as PRAGMATA pairs the two. These are
persistent-thread loops -- the name says so -- and it maps to
`NON_SEMANTIC_SIGNAL_CONCURRENT_WORKGROUP`, which is the forward-progress hint
such a loop wants. The fix was first confirmed on device without it; it is
included here because the shaders are the same shaders, and diverging from the
entry that already works for them needs a reason rather than an omission.

diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/device.c b/libs/vkd3d/device.c
index ff9a03f1..08cbc1e0 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/device.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/device.c
@@ -1054,8 +1054,21 @@ static const struct vkd3d_shader_quirk_info spiderman2_quirks = {
     spiderman2_hashes, ARRAY_SIZE(spiderman2_hashes), 0,
 };
 
-/* These shaders clamp the wave size to 32, but misses this in a few places of course ... */
-static const struct vkd3d_shader_quirk_hash pragmata_hashes[] = {
+/* These shaders clamp the wave size to 32, but misses this in a few places of course ...
+ *
+ * Vessel: shared with Resident Evil Requiem, which ships the same shaders.
+ * `PersistentClusterCulling` is byte-identical as an entry point name in both
+ * titles -- five compute shaders dumped from Requiem all carry it -- because it
+ * is RE Engine's own culling pass rather than anything per-game. Matching the
+ * shader by name instead of the executable is what makes one entry cover both,
+ * and any later RE Engine title that ships the pass unchanged.
+ *
+ * On a device whose subgroup is wider than the 32-thread group -- Adreno
+ * reports 64 -- the unclamped reads compute `base = waveSize * groupIdx` and
+ * stride by `waveSize`, so lane ranks cover 0..31 of a window advanced by 64
+ * and every second cluster is silently dropped. See docs/TODO.md #56.
+ */
+static const struct vkd3d_shader_quirk_hash re_engine_hashes[] = {
     {
         "PersistentClusterCulling", 0,
         VKD3D_SHADER_QUIRK_CLAMP_WAVE_SIZE_TO_THREAD_GROUP32 | VKD3D_SHADER_QUIRK_ENABLE_FAIR_SCHEDULING
@@ -1066,10 +1079,11 @@ static const struct vkd3d_shader_quirk_hash pragmata_hashes[] = {
     },
 };
 
-static const struct vkd3d_shader_quirk_info pragmata_quirks = {
-    pragmata_hashes, ARRAY_SIZE(pragmata_hashes), 0,
+static const struct vkd3d_shader_quirk_info re_engine_quirks = {
+    re_engine_hashes, ARRAY_SIZE(re_engine_hashes), 0,
 };
 
+
 static const struct vkd3d_shader_quirk_hash wow_hashes[] = {
     /* In addition to needing 64 byte descriptors, this ray query shader causes a heap OOB as well. */
     { NULL, 0xef2f620cbce5630c, VKD3D_SHADER_QUIRK_DESCRIPTOR_HEAP_ROBUSTNESS },
@@ -1192,7 +1206,9 @@ static const struct vkd3d_shader_quirk_meta application_shader_quirks[] = {
 	/* Spider Man 2 (2651280) */
     { VKD3D_STRING_COMPARE_EXACT, "Spider-Man2.exe", &spiderman2_quirks },
     /* PRAGMATA (3357650) */
-    { VKD3D_STRING_COMPARE_STARTS_WITH, "PRAGMATA", &pragmata_quirks },
+    { VKD3D_STRING_COMPARE_STARTS_WITH, "PRAGMATA", &re_engine_quirks },
+    /* Resident Evil Requiem -- same engine, same culling shaders. */
+    { VKD3D_STRING_COMPARE_EXACT, "re9.exe", &re_engine_quirks },
     /* Forza Horizon 6 (2483190). */
     { VKD3D_STRING_COMPARE_EXACT, "forzahorizon6.exe", &forza6_quirks },
     /* World of Warcraft */
